<title>AUSTRALIA: Qantas 7-month passenger growth 6.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Qantas 7-month passenger growth 6.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Qantas Airways Ltd said on Tuesday that passengers carried grew 6.6 percent to 11.05 million in the seven months to January 31.</p>
<p>Qantas, 25 percent owned by British Airways Plc, said revenue passenger kilometres (RPK) rose eight percent, while available seat kilometres (ASK) rose 8.9 percent over the seven month period. It said seat factors were 72.9 percent, slightly lower than the 1995/96 year to date level.</p>
<p>Domestic passenger growth was 3.3 percent for the period, while domestic RPK was 4.9 percent and ASK growth seven percent.  </p>
